WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.620
Tesla ended solar roof sales after installing roughly 3,000 units against a 1,000 per week target. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 632. The product page now redirects to standard solar panels. Intelligent living reports. There was no announcement. Reuters confirmed the decade-long program ended after 7 years of U.S. installations. The quiet shutdown came in August, 2026. Tesla had claimed the tiles would cost less than a conventional roof plus panels.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:32.160
The shortfall exceeded 95% of the volume goal.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.260
Solar roof tiles invert the usual relationship by making the tile itself the roof covering,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.100
with photovoltaic cells laminated inside.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:46.160
Almost all other rooftop solar uses building applied photovoltaics, where panels sit on top

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.060
of an existing roof held by racking.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:54.060
The category still faces physics, trade, money, and policy hurdles, even as some of those

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:54.840
factors shift.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:01.180
Integrated tiles have to satisfy roofing codes, electrical codes, structural loads, fire

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.420
ratings, and waterproofing all at once.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:07.320
They have to do that in custom sizes that vary from roof to roof.

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:12.480
That multi-code requirement raises per unit engineering and certification costs compared

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.120
with separate panels mounted on a conventional roof.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:20.380
When volume stays low, those fixed costs never spread across enough units to reach the

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.520
original price target.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.180
it. The integrated product could not compete on cost with standard panels plus a separate

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:31.420
roof, even before policy or installer skill constraints entered the picture. A weekly

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.760
pace that had been met would have produced more than 350,000 units. Two of the four hurdles

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.820
of physics, trades, money and policy have shifted since 2024, which changes the math for

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:48.720
any new entrant. Manufacturers chasing the same goal now includes solar facades, solar glazing

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.220
and flexible panels that adhere to any rooftop.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.320
The remaining markets sits with historic district and design-driven projects where appearance

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:01.040
commands a premium, unless someone else can solve the same integration problem at higher

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:01.500
volume.

